{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNQWeFyXzg8fJNu7y8eN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The filesystem half of the local executor now lives in a new `internal/executor/workspace` package, and the env policy is in package `executor`. `go test ./internal/executor/...` and `go vet` on those packages pass.\n\nI could not run a full `go test ./...` because the other modules need downloading and there is no network here. `servecmd`, `configcmd` and `committer` still build against the unchanged `local` API.\n\n- **CopyRole:** not added. Design revision 3 in the issue comments drops it, and the plan omits it. A maintainer should confirm.\n- **Docker flag:** `GOFLAGS=-buildvcs=false` was already in `runArgv` and is already described in `docs/proposal.md`, so nothing changed there.\n- **Local behaviour:** `local` keeps processes, Docker and tracking and calls `workspace` for the rest. If `ensureImage` or `ChmodReadOnly` fails after `Prepare` succeeds, it now calls `Discard`.\n- **Tests:** existing local tests changed only mechanically (fake git, clock and layout helpers now go through `Options` and `l.ws`). The cleanup, layout and scrub tests moved to `workspace`. I added tests for `Populate`, `FetchPinned`, `Discard`, `Prepare` rollback, foreign-repo `Remove` and the env policy.\n- **FetchPinned ref name:** it fetches a SHA into `refs/ard/pin`, where the old code used `refs/ard/sidecar/<sha>`. No test depends on the name.\n- **Rollback change:** `Prepare` now registers the home dir for rollback before it creates it. A failure while making the home therefore also removes it.\n\n`docs/layout.md` has the new workspace line and the updated local line. The report is in `.ard/313/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1176,"cache_read_input_tokens":87321,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_inp